  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Selenium (75Se) norcholesterol and Retinal dehydrogenase 1, mediated through a series of intermediate targets. The compound is linked to Corticosteroid 11-beta-dehydrogenase isozyme 2, which is in turn targeted by Papyramine and 7-Methoxy-3,7-Dimethyloctanal, both of which ultimately target Retinal dehydrogenase 1. This indicates a chain of interactions where Selenium (75Se) norcholesterol may influence the activity of these enzymes through a series of biochemical pathways. The scores from the paths suggest a strong, consistent relationship, but the exact mechanism by which Selenium (75Se) norcholesterol affects Retinal dehydrogenase 1 remains unclear. The evidence supports a possible regulatory role of the compound in the metabolic pathways involving these enzymes, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
